# AGENTS.md

Rules for AI coding assistants (Codex, Claude Code, Cursor, …) working in
[[ project_name ]]. Subdirectories may add their own `AGENTS.md`; the closest one wins
on conflict. [% if 'docs' in components %]Full standards: `docs/standards/` — read the linked document before
working in that area.
Project architecture and commands: `docs/standards/PROJECT.md`.[% endif %]

The sections above "Project-specific rules" are maintained by keel
(https://github.com/brizenchi/keel) and updated with `keel update`; edit the
project section freely.

## Must

- Pass the request context (cancellation, deadline, trace) through every call down
  to the database and outbound HTTP.
- Use structured logging with a fixed message and key/value fields; let the logger
  add `request_id`/`trace_id` from context. Never log secrets, tokens, request bodies
  or query strings.
- Handle each error once: add context and return it, or handle it at the boundary
  (HTTP handler, consumer, job). Map known errors to responses in one place; unknown
  errors log once at ERROR and return a generic message. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/CODE_STYLE.md`[% endif %]
[% if backend %]- HTTP APIs: `/api/v1` paths, one response envelope, correct status codes, a stable
  `reason` for errors the client must branch on, `page`/`limit`/`items`/`total`
  pagination, RFC 3339 UTC times, integer money in minor units. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/API_STANDARD.md`[% endif %]
- When an API changes, update its callers' types/clients in the same change.
- Database: never edit an applied migration; add a new one. Parameterized queries only;
  list queries have `LIMIT` and a stable order; expand → migrate → contract for
  breaking schema changes. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/DATABASE.md`[% endif %]
- Check resource ownership on every read/write; return 404 for other users' resources.
  [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/SECURITY_STANDARD.md`[% endif %]
[% endif %]- Add or update tests with every behaviour change; a bug fix starts with a failing test.
  No network access in tests. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/TESTING.md`[% endif %]
- Fake secrets in tests must look fake: `sk_test_not-a-real-key`, `whsec_not-a-real-secret`.
[%- if 'go' in languages %]

## Go
- `gofmt -s`; `go vet`; `go test -race`. `ctx context.Context` is the first parameter,
  never stored in structs; use `db.WithContext(ctx)` and `http.NewRequestWithContext`.
- Wrap errors with `fmt.Errorf("…: %w", err)`; compare with `errors.Is/As`; log with
  `slog.InfoContext(ctx, …)`. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/GO.md`[% endif %]
[%- endif %]
[%- if 'node' in languages %]

## Node / TypeScript
- Strict TypeScript, no `any`. All backend calls go through the shared API client; never
  call `fetch` from components. Show users messages derived from `status`/`reason`, never
  the raw server message; show the request id for 5xx. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/NODE.md`[% endif %]
- Browser-exposed env vars (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`) never contain secrets.
[%- endif %]
[%- if 'python' in languages %]

## Python
- `uv` for environments and dependencies (commit `uv.lock`); `ruff check` and
  `ruff format`; type hints on public functions; `pytest`.
- Raise domain exceptions with `from exc`; no bare `except:`. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/PYTHON.md`[% endif %]
[%- endif %]

## Must not

- Commit real secrets or `.env` files; print secrets in output.
- Push to `[[ default_branch ]]`, force-push, rewrite pushed history, or bypass hooks with `--no-verify`.
- Add a dependency without a stated reason [% if 'docs' in components %](`docs/standards/CI_QUALITY.md#dependencies`)[% endif %].
- Use panics/exceptions for expected business outcomes[% if backend %], or float types for money[% endif %].

## Commits and pull requests

Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject` (≤ 72 chars) — types
`feat fix perf refactor docs test build ci chore revert`. The PR title becomes the squash
commit. [% if 'docs' in components %]→ `docs/standards/GIT_WORKFLOW.md`[% endif %]

## Before finishing

Run the checks for the parts you changed[% if 'pr-template' in components %] (listed in
`.github/pull_request_template.md`)[% endif %] and report failures as they are; never claim
success without running them.

